      "eyebrow": "Why it matters",
      "heading": "Commissioning records are not optional",
      "html": "<p>Paperwork has always mattered for commercial and public HVAC. Building Regulations Part L and the CIBSE codes (Code A for air, Code W for water) say what to measure and record.</p><p>At home, grants changed the stakes. MCS MIS 3005 is the standard for heat pump installs. It says commission to the maker's instructions and keep the records. No records, no MCS registration. No registration, no grant. Most makers also refuse a warranty claim on a system that was not commissioned and recorded. The records protect the installer and the customer.</p>"
